  "strategy": "OPENING (2104): escort Santa Maria #9 to Wolf 359 and plant colony #3, convert Gliese 1's 47 res/yr into factories plus a permanent colonizer pipeline (Santa Maria + cheap Spore Clouds), and keep three scouts hunting habitable worlds - 60 planets is the win condition and I have 2.",
  "memo": "IRON FIST - STRATEGY MEMO (2104). PHASE: OPENING (2104-2118). VICTORY = 60 PLANETS OWNED, min game time 50 turns (2150). I have 2. Sprawl IS the war plan; the war fleet is what protects the sprawl later, not what wins now.\n\nSTATE: Gliese 1 (188,192) pop 35,800, 12/35 fact, 10/35 mine, 47 res/yr, surf 390/359/332, STARBASE - my only shipyard and my only refuelling point. Shaula (236,177) pop 8,900, 8 res/yr, surf 35/0/0 - it has ZERO surface boranium and germanium, so mines must precede factories there. Shaula is a 10-year investment, not a contributor.\n\nHARD LESSONS (do not repeat): Teamster #1 is permanently stranded at Shaula at 0 fuel - never send a freighter one-way to a starbase-less colony. Stalwart Defender #1 is down to 44/280 fuel from warp-6 hops; it goes to Wolf 359 at WARP 5 to stretch what is left. Fuel discipline is now a standing rule, not advice.\n\nTHIS TURN: Santa Maria #9 loads 2,500 colonists and runs Gliese 1 → Wolf 359 (294,176, hab 93%, conc 52/18/62), 107 ly at warp 6, three years. Stalwart Defender #1 goes ahead of it to kill e2's Armed Probe #1 sitting on that exact star. Wolf 359 is the only good unclaimed world scanned and it sits on the e2 approach lane - taking it is both expansion and a forward picket.\n\nTARGETS AFTER WOLF 359: every negative-hab rock counts toward 60. Megrez (0%), Mimosa (-1%), Groombridge 34 (-2%), Deneb (-2%), Kapteyn's (-3%), Zaurak (-4%), Betelgeuse (-5%). Take them with 22-res Spore Clouds once the factory base can feed a stream of them. Marginal worlds bleed population - accept it, they still count, and Biotech terraforming can be bought later if the count stalls.\n\nRECON: 79 stars unexplored - that is the real emergency, not e2. Scout #1 → Kochab (380,135, far east, e2 axis). Scout #2 → Rasalhague → Merak (south-east). Scout #8 → Alnitak (20,332, far south-west). I need habitable candidates faster than I need enemy intel.\n\nRESEARCH: 30% Propulsion. Better engines shorten every colony run, stop the fuel strandings that have already cost me a freighter, and carry the warships later. Switch to Weapons at ~2118 or the first sighting of an e2 warship, whichever is first. If the planet count stalls below ~10 by 2120, switch to Biotechnology for terraforming instead.\n\nQUEUES: Gliese 1 - Santa Maria x2, Factory x10, Spore Cloud x3, Factory x10, Mine x5. Shaula - Mine x4, Factory x5 (mines first, it has no germanium).\n\nSTANDING RULES:\n1. Two colonizers always in the Gliese 1 pipe. Never idle it.\n2. Factories before mines until Gliese 1 hits its pop cap on both.\n3. No warship spam before ~2120. A fleet with no economy loses the second battle.\n4. Warp 6 max for anything that is not a scout; warp 5 when fuel is under 25%.\n5. Nothing leaves home without return fuel or a starbase at the far end.\n6. Never send an unescorted colonizer past known enemy presence.\n7. TAKE worlds, never glass them - every planet is a point.\n8. Build an Orbital Fort at the second real colony as soon as it clears 20 res/yr, to get a forward refuelling node.\n\nOPEN: e2 homeworld unlocated (NE bearing). Wormhole Alpha found but reported with no coordinates. One galactic storm unlocated - do not route blind through unscanned space.",
